Subject: [PATCH 530/530] [DS4.1] Rejection-sampler benchmark: --dead-rows, the
 cut against the release's cap

Every request gets a dead-row cut. The TileLang kernels take it; the
baseline's verification does not, and its insertion caps the counts at it, as
the release served it. Before timing, ours are held bit for bit to themselves
on the drafts with the dead ones as placeholders, and the greedy requests'
counts and tokens to the baseline's.
---
 .../kernels/benchmark_tilelang_rejection.py   | 135 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 109 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)

